The round-0 solution, while containing many correct local computations (§2 machinery: atomicity, pushout kernels, fold calculus — MODULO lem:N's Step 2), has FATAL foundational gaps:
(A) It silently changes the problem's definition of monoid (adds f.g.) — the collapse lemma is false without it (lex-ℕ² / ℝ_{≥0} counterexamples), so this is not a cosmetic choice.
